  "final_text": "**Disposition:** ESCALATE, confidence 0.75. This is a proposal only; a human analyst decides.\n\n**Three facts that drove it:**\n1. The trader placed one BUY limit of 27,326 on SYN.A. That is 11.15 times average depth, 2 ticks from the touch, with nothing resting on the sell side. A SELL market order then executed 640 at 16:25:52.279.\n2. The BUY order had no fills before that sell. Its only fill was 4,707, after the sell. The remaining 22,619 was cancelled 704 ms after the sell. This is the \"caught in the book\" pattern in the escalation standard.\n3. Price moved 1.0 tick in the trader's favour and then reverted 1.5 ticks after the cancel. The trader is a prop trader with no registered market-making instruments. There was no market event, no risk event and no parent order, and 0 other participants cancelled in the second before the first cancel.\n\n**What would change my mind:** evidence that the 27,326 BUY was a genuine client or hedge order, or that the sell was an unrelated trade planned beforehand. Repeat cycles in other sessions would instead move this to DRAFT_STOR, which Level 2 would draft. This window holds a single cycle, and the trader has no prior alerts.",
